@startuml
title Planned Protection Cleanup (FST-028 / FST-050)
autonumber
participant "Session / rule change\nor shutdown" as Trigger
participant "Protection coordinator" as Coordinator
participant "Introduced-restriction registry" as Registry
participant "ApplicationBlockerPort" as Apps
participant "WebsiteBlockerPort" as Sites
participant "Local diagnostics / UI" as Feedback

Trigger -> Coordinator : pause, break, waiting, stop, shutdown,\nor rule disabled/deleted
Coordinator -> Coordinator : stop ineligible observations;\ncancel stale pending block decisions
Coordinator -> Registry : restrictions introduced for this scope
Registry --> Coordinator : application / website restriction handles
loop each introduced restriction
  alt application restriction
    Coordinator -> Apps : release introduced restriction
    Apps --> Coordinator : released / failed(reason)
  else website restriction
    Coordinator -> Sites : release introduced restriction
    Sites --> Coordinator : released / failed(reason)
  end
  alt released
    Coordinator -> Registry : remove restriction handle
  else failed
    Coordinator -> Registry : retain cleanup obligation
    Coordinator -> Feedback : report cleanup failure and recovery action
  end
end
note over Registry, Sites
  Never reverse restrictions created by another program/user.
  Concrete release/recovery behavior is adapter-specific and must
  be approved in FST-028/FST-050 before implementation.
end note
@enduml
